## 2. Ablation p-values unified with the language comparison (approved)
- New shared helper scripts/sign_permutation.py: two-sided exact sign-permutation test of the Wilcoxon signed-rank
  statistic over all 2^n_nz sign assignments, ties in |diff| handled by midranks (doubled ranks keep the DP integral),
  SciPy-version independent. Used by recompute_significance.py, eval_ablation_multirun.py and compute_language_stats.py.
- Why: SciPy `wilcoxon(method="exact")` uses the untied signed-rank table and is not exact when |diff| values tie
  (they do: per-query 5-run means take values in {0, 0.2, ..., 1}).
- Changes (only where ties exist):  no_fewshot 4.513e-12 -> 1.330e-12,  no_dict 1.049e-4 -> 9.918e-5,
  no_nbest 0.8125 -> 0.625 (0.75 in the first v23 package; see §8).  no_reranker 0.0195 / no_guard 1.000 / no_graph 0.1484 unchanged.
  Holm decisions unchanged (significant: no_fewshot, no_dict; no_reranker Holm p = 0.0781 unchanged).
- Independently re-derived by the author (midrank DP) — identical values.
- Canonical files: evaluation/ablation_multirun_stats.json (per-condition `significance_tests.<cond>.test =
  sign-permutation-exact-midranks`; the file-level `_meta` block was added only in §10 — an earlier revision of this
  log wrongly claimed it existed here), evaluation/significance_recomputed.json (`_meta.test_label`; primary p_value = sign-permutation; `p_value_scipy_exact_untied` and
  `p_value_approx_legacy` are recomputed audit values; `p_value_stored_before_run` = value found in
  ablation_multirun_stats.json when the script ran — this key was named `legacy_p_value` until the fresh-extraction
  check below showed that a re-run silently overwrote it with the already-unified value; renamed so the audit
  meaning is unambiguous and `--apply` is idempotent, commit 5305d7db).
  Regenerated SSOT -> Table 1 / Fig. 3 caption / §2.5 / §4.7 / S10 text.
- Language comparison (p = 0.193, bootstrap CI) byte-identical; all six PNG figures byte-identical to baseline-v22.

