## 8. Post-review correction: float-representation ties in sign_permutation (commits 37d45a95, f80ac54c)
- Finding (Devin Review on PR #578): `rankdata([abs(d) ...])` ranked mathematically equal differences separately when
  their binary representations differ. Per-query 5-run means produce e.g. 0.2 and 1.0-0.8 = 0.19999999999999996; in the
  stored no_nbest data the five non-zero differences are [-0.0383, 0.2, 0.1820, -0.2, 0.19999999999999996], so the three
  |diff| = 0.2 received midranks 3.5 / 5 / 3.5 instead of a shared 4, giving p = 0.75 instead of 0.625.
- Fix: `scripts/sign_permutation.py` rounds |diff| to TIE_DECIMALS = 9 before midranking. Regression test
  `test_float_representations_of_equal_diffs_share_a_midrank` (both representations -> 0.625). Suite 165 -> 166.
- Effect: only no_nbest changes (0.75 -> 0.625; Holm 1.000, n.s. — no decision changes). no_fewshot / no_dict /
  no_reranker / no_guard / no_graph byte-identical. `p_value_scipy_exact_untied` (0.8125) kept as audit value.
- Regenerated: evaluation/ablation_multirun_stats.json, evaluation/significance_recomputed.json, paper/paper_data.json
  (n_unit_tests 165 -> 166), stam-m_ja.tex (Table 1 row 0.7500 -> 0.6250, §4.1 p = 0.625, S1 / Data availability / S10
  test count 166, S1 sign-permutation category 3 -> 4 tests), README_SQL.md, freeze artifacts (SHA256SUMS_ja.txt,
  ja_numbers.tsv 2,035 lines), tag ja-final moved ab25c94d -> f80ac54c. PDF rebuilt: 30 pages, undefined 0, overfull 8 (TikZ).
- Package rebuilt from f80ac54c (build_sql_package.py, GIT_COMMIT = f80ac54c; 1527 files) and re-verified from a fresh
  extraction of the rebuilt ZIP (1573 files):
  - verify_all --static-only PASS=8 ; verify_all --warnings-as-errors PASS=18 WARN=0 FAIL=0 SKIP=0
  - pytest 166 passed ; ruff clean ; verify_ssot 5/5 ; verify_paper_numbers --tex stam-m_ja.tex exit 0 gating 0 ;
    default (both TeX) exit 1 as expected ; SHA256SUMS_ja 13/13 OK
