## 9. Post-merge correction: verify_all provenance keys may not be omitted (PR #579, commits e9c34c1e, 120adf18)
- Finding (Devin Review on PR #578, scripts/verify_all.py check_provenance): the dataset<->provenance directory
  comparison and the downstream gold_sha256 / expected_sha256 checks were all gated on
  isinstance(prov[dir_key], str). A provenance block that omitted gold_dir(+gold_sha256) or
  expected_dir(+expected_sha256) therefore passed with those inputs unverified although the dataset rows point
  at a concrete directory. A second Devin Review pass on PR #579 noted the same bypass one level up: with
  dataset_file itself omitted, dataset_rows stayed empty and none of the directory checks ran.
- Fix: every provenance block must carry a string dataset_file and dataset_sha256 (build_provenance() always emits
  both; all 32 shipped blocks have them). When the dataset rows resolve to a directory, a missing dir key is an error ("provenance gold_dir is
  missing"), and a present dir with a missing hash key is an error ("provenance gold_sha256 is missing ...").
  Datasets without gold_sql_path / expected_result_path rows (pre-R22 provenance) are unaffected.
- Regression assertions (dataset_file / dataset_sha256 / gold_dir / gold_sha256 / expected_dir / expected_sha256 stripped
  in turn -> VerifyError; a git_commit-only block -> VerifyError; full block -> PASS) were appended to
  tests/test_evaluation_metrics.py::test_verify_all_provenance_new_keys_tamper_detection, so the suite stays at
  166 and the frozen manuscript / SSOT test count (ja-final = f80ac54c) is untouched.
- Effect on shipped data: none. All 32 provenance blocks already carry all six keys; no evaluation artifact, SSOT,
  figure, TeX or freeze file changes. Only sql_package/scripts/verify_all.py, sql_package/tests/
  test_evaluation_metrics.py and GIT_COMMIT (f80ac54c -> 120adf18) differ from the v23 package.
- Package rebuilt from 120adf18 (build_sql_package.py, 1527 files) and re-verified from a fresh extraction of
  the rebuilt ZIP (results appended below by the gate run).
  - verify_all --static-only PASS=8 ; verify_all --warnings-as-errors PASS=18 WARN=0 FAIL=0 SKIP=0 (raw output ->
    verification_logs/verify_all_dbfull.log, replaced)
