## 12. verify_all provenance: gold/expected dir+hash keys required unconditionally (PR #581, commit 41e86c06)
- Devin Review on the merged PR #579 (comment 3998661582): check_provenance() derived the set of parent directories
  `dirs` from the dataset rows' gold_sql_path / expected_result_path and only demanded gold_dir / gold_sha256 /
  expected_dir / expected_sha256 when `dirs` was non-empty. For a dataset whose rows carry no paths
  (e.g. {"id":"q1","question":"x"}) every branch was skipped and the later hash checks are isinstance(str)-gated, so a
  block missing all four keys still passed. build_provenance() always emits the four keys, so their absence is never
  legitimate. Reproduced with the new test assertions against the pre-fix code (DID NOT RAISE VerifyError).
- Fix (scripts/verify_all.py): the four keys are required as strings on every block, independent of the dataset rows;
  the parent-directory consistency check (single dir, equal to the recorded one) still runs additionally when rows
  carry paths. Regression assertions appended inside test_verify_all_provenance_new_keys_tamper_detection (path-less
  dataset, each key stripped in turn -> VerifyError; full block -> PASS), so the suite stays at 166 (the count frozen
  in stam-m_ja.tex / paper_data.json.testing).
- No data, SSOT, figure, manuscript or frozen file changed; ja-final (f80ac54c) not moved; SHA256SUMS_ja.txt unchanged.
  All 32 shipped provenance blocks already carry the four keys, so verify_all results are unchanged.
